\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 The word of the Great Teacher was heard; the Elvi went forth.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 They went forth straight from the Clambake to the backs seats and bonnets of Cadillacs and Lincolns, to Ford Probes and Escorts, to Hummers and Dodge Swingers, even to Honda Fits, though none who spoke Spanish resorted to Mazda Laputa\'92s or Mitsubishi Pajero\'92s.\
They heeded the words of the Great Teacher behind dumpsters and in phone booths. They heeded his words in bars and laundromats, in gyms and movie theatres, in supermarkets and jewellery stores, in book clubs and seances, in kitchens and bathrooms, in back alleys and rooftop gardens, in burger joints and ice cream parlours.\
Wherever they went, they spread the word of the Great Teacher and the word was, \'93Hump and you shall be saved! Praise the Dawkins and the Holy Momma!\'94\
Elvi held karaoke and sex parties that became known as Humpenings. They held them in private homes and community halls and old libraries that had never seen such attendances nor such flagrant flouting of the silent study zones. Reading tables were desecrated and book shelves toppled over. Some pages were dog-eared. Librarians were scandalised to the point of ecstasy.\
The frenzy continued for days.\
Yet Elvi still fell sick and died.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 \'93Excuse me, sir,\'94 Fisher interrupted, while averting his eyes. \'93The cloakroom is filled to capacity and guests are throwing their clothes off in the lift lobby.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Chanta had to unlock his face from an Elvine whose name he could only guess at (probably Sister Michelle, and she was definitely changing habits). \'93Take the night off, Fisher. We\'92ll figure the laundry out tomorrow.\'94\
\'93Yes, sir. May I retire to my quarters?\'94\
\'93Of course, Fisher you ol\'92 dog.\'94\
\'93Yes, sir. I am afraid I am quite fatigued after five nights of this.\'94\
Chanta had thrown the reception room of his Starborne One penthouse open. In \'93Hump Mode\'94 (which involved very close proximity and at least several \'93high-density pile-ups\'94) he could host slightly shy of eight hundred guests. There was a bandstand but no one performed on it, at least not any performance that was in the least music-adjacent. The karaoke machine had malfunctioned three days earlier and was playing \'93My Way\'94 on repeat. No one sang because everyone was too busy doing it their way. There was almost no conversation, just the occasional, \'93Thank you very much\'94.\
Chanta\'92s continuous Humpening was so popular, the High Elvis organised a lottery system and buses to shuttle guests between the Ghetto and Chanta\'92s tower.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 On the seventh day they rested. The High Elvis summoned Chanta and the Holy Aunts to Parliament to discuss progress. Elvi were still falling sick and dying.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Aunt Kathy had answers.
